# =============================================================================
#  Release signing configuration -- EXAMPLE / TEMPLATE  (safe to commit)
# =============================================================================
#
#  This is the public template for the real file desifit/android/key.properties.
#  Local release-signing setup:
#    1. Copy this file to "key.properties" in this directory.
#    2. Replace every placeholder below with your real values.
#    3. Put your keystore where `storeFile` points (default: android/app/key.jks).
#
#  THE FOUR KEYS BELOW ARE A CONTRACT. They are exactly what
#  android/app/build.gradle.kts reads in signingConfigs "release", and what the
#  "Configure Production Signing" step of .github/workflows/android_release.yml
#  writes. Do not add, rename, or remove keys here without updating both
#  consumers in lockstep.
#
#  Where each value comes from:
#    storePassword   local: keystore password       CI: secret PLAY_STORE_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD
#    keyPassword     local: key password            CI: secret PLAY_STORE_KEY_PASSWORD
#    keyAlias        local: key alias               CI: secret PLAY_STORE_KEY_ALIAS
#    storeFile       local: path to your .jks       CI: key.jks (decoded from PLAY_STORE_KEYSTORE_BASE64)
#
#  SECURITY -- never commit real signing material:
#    * key.properties and android/app/key.jks are git-ignored (android/.gitignore
#      plus the root .gitignore rules). If `git status` ever lists them as
#      untracked, do NOT `git add` them.
#    * CI never sees your keystore in the repo: the workflow base64-decodes the
#      secret into android/app/key.jks at build time and the file is never
#      uploaded or persisted.
#    * To rotate credentials, update the repository Actions secrets (Settings ->
#      Secrets and variables -> Actions), never this template.
#
#  Placeholders only -- keep this file free of real values:
storePassword=your_keystore_password
keyPassword=your_key_password
keyAlias=your_key_alias
storeFile=key.jks
